    "result_text": "All green. The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the audit log confirms the fiscal-year membership number (`...-M27` for a 2026-09-02 registration).\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved date-derived values to a fiscal-year basis (FY starts 1 July, numbered by its ending calendar year, so 1 Jul 2026 \u2013 30 Jun 2027 = FY27).\n\n**New cohesive unit** \u2014 `FiscalYear.java` (one tiny class, all new fiscal-year logic in one place):\n- `of(date)` \u2192 fiscal year number (`month \u2265 7 ? year+1 : year`)\n- `label(owner)` \u2192 `FY<YY>` from the (already business-day-adjusted) registration date\n- `yy(owner)` \u2192 two-digit fiscal year for the membership identifier\n\n**Behaviour wired in with minimal edits to existing functions:**\n- `OwnerMapper` \u2014 membershipNumber year segment now uses `FiscalYear.yy(owner)`; added a `fiscalYear` mapping returning `FY<YY>` (2 annotation lines on a body-less method).\n- `SaveOwner` \u2014 audit membershipNumber uses `FiscalYear.yy(owner)`, keeping the identifier consistent with the DTO (1 line).\n- `MembershipPoints` \u2014 the tenure bonus now counts elapsed fiscal years (`> 1`) instead of a 365-day window (1 line in the scoring method; the private helper rewritten).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `fiscalYear` schema property and refreshed the two affected descriptions (docs only, no function cost).\n\n**Keeping structural impact low:** the only truly changed existing method with any complexity is `MembershipPoints.of`, touched at a single line. Everything genuinely new lives in one small standalone class, so no existing method or class grew, and each edit sits in a low-`WMC_other` context.\n\nThe spec's behaviour change is intentional and now reflected: the membership identifier's year segment and tenure both use the fiscal year rather than calendar year / 365-day windows.",
